# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully implemented Vercel Speed Insights for the UMBC Food Radar static HTML website.

## Changes Made

### Modified Files:
- **web_scrapper/index.html** - Added Vercel Speed Insights tracking scripts

## Implementation Details

Since this is an HTML/JavaScript static site project deployed on Vercel, I followed the HTML framework implementation pattern from the Vercel Speed Insights documentation:

1. **Added Speed Insights Script Tags**: Added two script tags before the closing `</body>` tag in `index.html`:
   - First script: Initializes the `window.si` function to queue Speed Insights events
   - Second script: Loads the Speed Insights tracking script from `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js` with defer attribute

The implementation follows the exact pattern recommended in the Vercel documentation for HTML sites and is placed alongside the existing Vercel Web Analytics script that was already in the project.

## Notes
- No package installation was required for the HTML implementation (as noted in the documentation)
- The Speed Insights script will be automatically available at `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js` after the next deployment to Vercel
- Speed Insights must be enabled in the Vercel dashboard project settings for the tracking to work
- The implementation is non-blocking (uses `defer` attribute) to avoid impacting page load performance
- This implementation will start tracking Core Web Vitals metrics (LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, TTFB, INP) once deployed

## Next Steps for User
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Speed Insights → Enable)
2. Deploy this change to Vercel
3. After deployment, verify the script loads by checking for `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js` in the page source
4. View metrics in the Vercel dashboard after visitors start using the site
